# The server-rendered pages come first: they are real paths on the public domain, and
# the SPA catch-all below would otherwise swallow them and answer with index.html.
#
# They are rendered by the API (server/src/seo/), which in production is a different
# origin — so they have to be proxied here, or they end up as a second website on the
# API's hostname competing with this one. See PRODUCTION.md, "City landing pages,
# robots.txt and sitemap.xml".
#
# The dev server proxies this same set; see `server.proxy` in vite.config.ts. Change one
# and change the other, or a link works in dev and 404s in production.

# Listing photos (and the city-page session check) are stored as site-relative
# `/api/v1/...` paths. The client talks to the API by its own origin, so without
# this the catch-all below answers an <img> with index.html and the gallery is blank.
# Vite proxies `/api` the same way; see `server.proxy` in vite.config.ts.
/api/*         https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/api/:splat             200

# The front door is HTML from the API, like the city pages. Exact `/` only: the
# splat below is what serves the app everywhere else.
#
# The bang is required. `/` also matches the published index.html, and without it
# Netlify serves that file and a crawler reads an empty canonical and the title
# "Urban365".
/              https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/                       200!

/nadlan        https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/nadlan                  200
/nadlan/*      https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/nadlan/:splat           200
/blog          https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/blog                    200
/blog/*        https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/blog/:splat             200
/sitemap.xml   https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/sitemap.xml             200
/sitemap-*     https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/sitemap-:splat          200
/robots.txt    https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/robots.txt              200
/llms.txt      https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/llms.txt                200
/llms-full.txt https://urban365-production.up.railway.app/llms-full.txt           200

# SPA: every other path (e.g. /agency/6816047?listing=…) is served by index.html and
# resolved client-side by react-router.
/*    /index.html   200
